## Rows skipped
- a#23 — "TWD 1.57M". ACCEPTED-lv: test-pinned, byte-identical. Not reformatted to "1,57 milj."
- b#21 — space thousands ("1 579 589") and "milj." R14: Latvian thousands stay a dot. The checker rejects a space as the thousands separator. Amounts such as TWD 1.579.589 left as dots.
- Frontmatter `url:` Hangul in 008 and 009 (R16). Fullwidth colon inside the 008 url left as-is.
- Date stamps. ACCEPTED-lv says change "13. septembrī 2025" to "2025. gada 13. septembris" only if the checker still parses, otherwise keep. Nominative "septembris" is not in the month lexicon. The registered year-first pattern does match "2025. gada 13. septembrī", but stripStructuralNoise treats a line-initial "YYYY. " as a markdown ordered-list marker (the token after the dot is "gada", not a month) and deletes the year before the date parser runs. Missing numbers were 9 and the year. Restored the form the checker accepts: "13. septembrī 2025" (16 files), "4. februārī 2026" (011), "17. septembrī 2026" (018). In-sentence "2026. gada 1. jūlijā" and similar stay; they are not at line start.
- R2b Korea-tax framing in 001 and 004 was already present ("Šis izklāsts attiecas uz lietas apstākļiem ar saikni ar Koreju… nav visiem ieguldītājiem… Jūsu izcelsmes valsti"). Not duplicated.
